From 0bc4df24bc1dae66bae1721780ea5b68a35be353 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:29:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a remote card's notice wakes an idle chat
 instead of only writing a row [daveey] (#220)

On 2026-10-29 two hub cards' done notices were written into idle David-MBP chat 20261027_134353_5ab65c
on time (15:24:56Z, 16:53:29Z) as passive kanban_notice rows. No turn ran until a local card's notice
woke the chat at 18:58Z, 2-3.5 h later. The unloaded sweeper wakes chats for local cards. The remote
sweep in the same loop only appended the row.

The production sweeper now passes a _RemoteWaker. A fresh remote notice gets the same grace window
the local sweep gives (the chat's live poller claims first). It is then claimed in the remote ledger,
the way collect() claims it, and starts ONE turn under the same skip rules, wake budget and slots.
A refused or failed wake writes the passive row. A turn in flight releases the claim for the next pass.
Calls without a waker (tests, tools) keep the passive-row behaviour.

Card: hub t_01a18933349f9cdf
